.TH AVR\-SETTINGS\-SET 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-settings-set \- Set a setting value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr settings set
[OPTIONS] KEY VALUE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a setting value.
.PP
VALUE is parsed as a boolean (true/false) or integer when possible, otherwise treated as a string.
.PP
Writes a repository override when run inside a connected checkout (the repo is auto-detected), when --repo is given, or when AVR_REPO is set. Otherwise targets org scope (the default org, or --org); org-only settings must be set with --org. A checkout whose repo isn't connected to the org is an error rather than a silent org-wide write.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr settings set cache.gha.enabled false --org org-abc123
    avr settings set cache.packages.enabled true --repo rep-xyz789
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIKEY\fR
\&
.TP
\fIVALUE\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git unless --org given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-settings (1),
.BR avr-settings-list (1),
.BR avr-settings-reset (1),
.BR avr-settings-schema (1)
